[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: System Requirements
UID: YAAP-SR
DATE: @GIT_COMMIT_DATETIME
PREFIX: SR-

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Introduction

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This document defines the system requirements for Yet Another Audio Player (Yaap),
a time accurate desktop audio player.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Main App

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Audio Playback

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Audio Format Support

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-001
TITLE: FLAC Audio Support
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall support playback of audio files encoded in the FLAC format.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-002
TITLE: MP3 Audio Support
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall support playback of audio files encoded in the MP3 format.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-003
TITLE: WAV Audio Support
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall support playback of audio files containing supported PCM audio 
in the WAV container format.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-004
TITLE: AAC Audio Support
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall support playback of audio files encoded in the AAC codec in 
supported containers, including M4A audio files.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-005
TITLE: ALAC Audio Support
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall support playback of audio files encoded in the ALAC format.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-006
TITLE: Vorbis Audio Support
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall support playback of audio files encoded in the Vorbis codec in
supported containers, including OGG files.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-007
TITLE: Opus Audio Support
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall support playback of audio files encoded in the Opus codec in 
supported containers.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-008
TITLE: AIFF Audio Support
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall support playback of audio files containing supported PCM audio 
in the AIFF container format.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-001

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: General Audio Decoding

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-009
TITLE: Audio Format Identification
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall identify the audio format of an input file using its content or 
format metadata rather then relying solely on its file extension.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-010
TITLE: Unsupported Audio Formats
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall report when an audio file cannot be played because its format or
encoding is unsupported.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-011
TITLE: Invalid Audio Files
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall report an appropriate error when an audio file cannot be decoded
because its contents are invalid or corrupted.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-002

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Local Audio Files

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-012
TITLE: Local Audio File Selection
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall allow for a local audio file to be browsed or selected for playback.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-013
TITLE: Local Audio File Playback
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall play a selected local audio file when its format and encoding 
are supported.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-014
TITLE: Local File Access Failure
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall report when a selected local audio file cannot be accessed for 
playback.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-003

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Cloud Provider Support

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-015
TITLE: Cloud Provider Support
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall support connecting to Google Drive, iCloud Drive, Dropbox,
and Microsoft OneDrive.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-016
TITLE: Cloud Provider Authentication
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall support authenticating with a supported cloud storage provider.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-017
TITLE: Cloud Connection Status
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall report whether a cloud storage connection has been established
successfully.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-018
TITLE: Cloud Connection Failure
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall report an appropriate error when a connection to a cloud storage
provider cannot be established.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-004

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Remote Audio Files

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-019
TITLE: Remote Audio File Selection
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall allow for audio files to be browsed or selected for playback
through a connected cloud storage provider.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-020
TITLE: Remote Audio File Playback
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall play a selected remote audio file when its format and encoding are
supported and the file is accessible.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-021
TITLE: Remote File Access Failure
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall report when a selected remote audio file cannot be retrieved
for playback.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-022
TITLE: Remote Playback Interruption
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall report when a remote audio file becomes unavailable during playback
and playback cannot continue.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-005

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Audio Quality

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-023
TITLE: Audio Decoding Fidelity
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall decode supported audio files according to their encoding format 
without introducing additional lossy encoding during decoding.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-006

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Audio Playback Position

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-024
TITLE: Playback Position Accuracy
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall make the current playback position of the active audio track 
available to the user.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-025
TITLE: Playback Position Accuracy
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall report the playback position within the specified timing accuracy 
under defined operating conditions.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-026
TITLE: Elapsed Playback Time
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall report the elapsed playback time of the active audio track, 
corresponding to its current playback position.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-007
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-027
TITLE: Playback Position Seeking
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall allow the user to request a playback position within the duration 
of the active audio track.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-009

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-028
TITLE: Seek Position Accuracy
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall seek to the requested playback position with the greatest accuracy 
supported by the active audio track and playback pipeline, targeting a maximum 
error of 1 microsecond where supported.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-009

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-029
TITLE: Remaining Playback Time
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall display the estimated remaining playback time of the active audio
track, calculated from its duration and current playback position.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-010

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-030
TITLE: Media Playback Information
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall make the currently playing track's available playback information 
accessible through the operating system's media-control interface.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-011

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-031
TITLE: Media Playback Information
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall make the currently playing track's metadata accessible through 
the operating system's media-control interface, where supported hby that interface.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-011

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-032
TITLE: Media Playback Controls
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall support playback control commands received through the operating 
system's media-control interface, where supported by that interface.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-011

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Audio Playback Customization

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-033
TITLE: Playback Speed Adjustment
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall support the adjustment of the playback speed of the active 
audio track.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-012

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-034
TITLE: Playback Speed Range
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall support playback speeds within a range of 0.5x to 2.0x at minimum.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-012

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-035
TITLE: Independent Playback Pitch Adjustment
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall support the adjustment of the playback pitch independently of 
playback speed.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-013

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-036
TITLE: Playback Pitch Range
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall support playback pitch changes within a range of ±6 semitones
at minimum.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-013

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-037
TITLE: Playback Volume Adjustment
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall support the adjustment of the playback volume within a range 
of 0% to 150%.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-014

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-038
TITLE: Audio Processing Configuration
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall allow the user to configure each supported audio processing option.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-015

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-039
TITLE: Active Playback Customisation Information
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall make the currently active playback speed, pitch adjustment, 
volume setting and audio processing options available for display to the user.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-016

[[/SECTION]]

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Audio Tracks

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Track Metadata

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-040
TITLE: Displaying Track Metadata
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall allow for the viewing of available metadata for a selected
audio track.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-027

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-041
TITLE: Editing Track Metadata
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall allow for the modification of metadata fields that are editable 
for a selected audio track.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-028

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-042
TITLE: Editing Track Metadata
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall allow for the deletion of metadata fields that are editable 
for a selected audio track.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-028

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-043
TITLE: Saving Track Metadata
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall allow metadata changes made to an audio track to be saved.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-029

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-044
TITLE: Reporting Metadata Save Results
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall report if metadata changes were saved successfully.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-029

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-045
TITLE: Reporting Metadata Save Results
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall report an error if atempting to save metadata changes fails.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-029

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-046
TITLE: Identifying Non-Editable Metadata Fields
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall distinguish metadata fields that cannot be modified from fields 
that can be modified.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-030

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Undoing and Redoing Actions

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-125
TITLE: Undoing Track Metadata Changes
STATEMENT: The system shall support undoing track metadata changes.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-105

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-126
TITLE: Redoing Track Metadata Changes
STATEMENT: The system shall support redoing track metadata changes.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-105

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Tags

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-047
TITLE: Creating Tags
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall allow for the creation tags for use in organising audio files,
playlists and collections.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-022

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-048
TITLE: Deleting Tags
STATEMENT: The system shall allow for the deletion of tags.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-022

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-049
TITLE: Removing Deleted Tags
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall remove deleted tags from any audio files, playlists
or collections that are using them.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-022

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-133
TITLE: Undoing Tag Changes
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall support undoing playlist and collection metadata changes, 
provided the previous state can be restored.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-082

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-134
TITLE: Redoing Tag Changes
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall support redoing playlist and collection metadata changes, 
provided the previous state can be restored.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-083

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-050
TITLE: Tag Persistence
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall preserve tags and their assignments across application sessions.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-022

[[/SECTION]]

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Audio Library

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Adding Local Files

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-051
TITLE: Local Audio File Selection
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall allow for selected local audio files to be added to the library.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-017

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-052
TITLE: Adding Local Audio Files
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall add selected supported local audio files to the library.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-017

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-053
TITLE: Handling Inaccessible Local Files
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall report an error when a selected local audio file cannot be 
accessed or added to the library.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-017

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Adding Remote Files

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-054
TITLE: Remote Audio File Selection
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall allow for selected audio files from connected cloud storage 
providers to be added to the library.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-018

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-055
TITLE: Adding Remote Audio Files
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall add selected supported remote audio files to the library.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-018

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-056
TITLE: Handling Inaccessible Remote Files
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall report an error when a selected remote audio file cannot be 
accessed or added to the library.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-017

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Removing Files

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-057
TITLE: Preserving Source Audio Files
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall allow for the removal of a audio files from the library without 
deleting the underlying audio file.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-019

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-058
TITLE: Deleting Source Audio Files
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall allow for the deletion of a audio files from the underlying 
storage.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-019

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Browsing Files

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-059
TITLE: Library Browsing
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall present the audio files in the library for
browsing and selection.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-020

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-060
TITLE: Library Persistence
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall preserve library entries across application sessions.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-104

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-061
TITLE: Handling Unavailable Library Files
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall retain library entries when their associated audio 
files become unavailable.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-104

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-062
TITLE: Differentiating Unavailable Library Files
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall differentiate unavailable audio files from available audio files.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-104

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Undoing and Redoing Actions

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-131
TITLE: Undoing Library Changes
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall support undoing library changes, provided the 
previous state can be restored.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-021

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-132
TITLE: Redoing Library Changes
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall support redoing library changes, provided 
the previous state can be restored.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-021

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Searching, Sorting, Filtering and Tagging

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-063
TITLE: Removing Tags from Audio Files
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall allow for the removal of tag assignments from audio files in 
the library without deleting the tags themselves.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-022

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-064
TITLE: Assigning Tags to Audio Files
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall allow for existing tags to be assigned to audio files in 
the library.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-022

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-065
TITLE: Searching Library Tracks
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall allow for the searching of tracks in the library using tags or 
supported track attributes.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-023

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-066
TITLE: Empty Search Results
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall indicate when a library search returns no matching tracks.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-026

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-067
TITLE: Sorting Library Tracks
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall allow the user to sort library tracks by supported track attributes.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-024

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-068
TITLE: Filtering Library Tracks
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall allow the user to filter library tracks using supported track 
attributes.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-025

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-069
TITLE: Empty Filter Results
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall indicate when filtering the library returns no matching tracks.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-026

[[/SECTION]]

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Playlists and Collections

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Playlist Modification

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-070
TITLE: Creating Playlists
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall allow for the creation of playlists.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-031

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-071
TITLE: Adding Tracks to Playlists
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall allow for the addition of tracks from the library to a playlist.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-032

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-072
TITLE: Duplicate Playlist Entries
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall allow the same track to appear multiple times within a playlist.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-032

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-073
TITLE: Removing Tracks from Playlists
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall allow the user to remove individual track entries from a 
playlist without removing the corresponding tracks from their library.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-033

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-074
TITLE: Modifying Playlist Metadata
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall allow the user to modify editable metadata fields for playlists.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-035

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-075
TITLE: Persisting Playlists
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall preserve playlists, including their membership, ordering and 
editable metadata, across application sessions.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-036

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Collection Modification

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-076
TITLE: Creating Playlists
STATEMENT: The system shall allow for the creation of collections.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-031

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-077
TITLE: Adding Playlists and Collections to Collections
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall allow the user to add playlists and collections to a collection.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-032

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-078
TITLE: Preventing Circular Collections
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall prevent the addition of a collection to itself or to any of its 
descendant collections.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-079
TITLE: Removing Items from Collections
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall allow the user to remove playlists and collections from a 
collection without deleting the referenced playlists or collections.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-033

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-080
TITLE: Modifying Collection Metadata
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall allow the user to modify editable metadata fields for collections.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-035

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-081
TITLE: Persisting Playlists and Collections
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall preserve collections, including their membership, ordering and 
editable metadata, across application sessions.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-036

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Undoing and Redoing Actions

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-82
TITLE: Undoing Playlist and Collection Changes
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall support undoing playlist and collection changes, provided the 
previous state can be restored.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-102

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-83
TITLE: Redoing Playlist and Collection Changes
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall support redoing playlist and collection changes, provided 
the previous state can be restored.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-102

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-84
TITLE: Undoing Playlist and Collection Metadata Changes
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall support undoing playlist and collection metadata changes, 
provided the previous state can be restored.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-103

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-85
TITLE: Redoing Playlist and Collection Metadata Changes
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall support redoing playlist and collection metadata changes, 
provided the previous state can be restored.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-103

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Searching, Sorting, Filtering and Tagging

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-086
TITLE: Removing Tags from Audio Files
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall allow for the removal of tag assignments from audio files in 
a playlist without deleting the tags themselves.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-037

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-087
TITLE: Removing Tags from playlists and collections 
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall allow for the removal of tag assignments from a playlist or 
collection without deleting the tags themselves.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-037

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-088
TITLE: Assigning Tags to Audio Files
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall allow for existing tags to be assigned to audio files in 
a playlist.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-037

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-089
TITLE: Assigning Tags to playlists and collections
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall allow for existing tags to be assigned to playlists and
collections.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-037

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-090
TITLE: Searching Playlist Tracks
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall allow for the searching of tracks in a playlist using tags or 
supported track attributes.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-038

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-091
TITLE: Searching Collections for Playlists
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall allow for the searching of playlists in a collection using 
tags or supported attributes.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-038

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-092
TITLE: Searching Collections for Collections
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall allow for the searching of collections in a collection using 
tags or supported attributes.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-038

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-093
TITLE: Empty Search Results
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall indicate when a playlist or collection search returns no 
matching tracks.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-041

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-094
TITLE: Sorting Playlist Tracks
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall allow the user to sort playlist tracks using supported track 
